# @@{project_name} hub

Workspace hub of the @@{project_name} project (`@@{project_hub_repo}`): every change to its repos goes through it.

- `hub.json`: the project config (repos, tracker, branch prefix, checks, guard paths)
- Files rendered from `hub.json` and rewritten by `hub sync`: listed in `AGENTS.md`, which `hub sync` keeps current
- This README and the other seeded files are created once, then owned by the project
- `brain/`: curated, versioned project memory (start at `brain/index.md`)

`make help` lists the entry points.

Agents' Bash runs in Claude Code's sandbox, on purpose: writes stay in the workspace, the network is an HTTP(S)
allowlist and SSH never passes. The hub's own network commands (`git fetch`/`push`, `gh`, `./hub worktree`) are
excluded, but only as a bare Bash call. A `Broken pipe` or `Operation not permitted` from an agent's git or uv is the
sandbox, not your access; `./hub doctor` checks the setup (rule `sandbox.workflow`).

Repos, checked out next to this hub: @@{repo_dirs}.

Each repo's root `AGENTS.md` (`hub agent` loads it) starts as a copy of `docs/app-repo-AGENTS.md`, filled in.

## Join this hub

Follow these steps once per machine to work on @@{project_name} from this hub.

### Requirements

| Tool | Needed | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) 0.9 or newer | required | runs `./hub` (through uv); fetches Python 3.14 |
| `git` | required | clones the hub and its repos; worktrees, commits, pushes |
| [Claude Code](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code) (`claude`) | required | the agent sessions `./agent` starts |
| `python3` 3.9 or newer | required | `./hub` reads `hub.json` with it; the hooks (guard, brief, stop gate) run on it |
| [`gh`](https://cli.github.com/) | optional | `gh auth setup-git`, and the auth, PR and CI lines of `./hub brief` |
| tracker credential | optional | `./hub next` and `./hub run` read the tracker (the Tracker line below) |

### Access

`./hub` fetches the agent-hub platform, which is public (unless `hub.json` → `platform.repository` names another).
This hub (`@@{project_hub_repo}`) and its repos need your own GitHub access through a git credential helper (e.g.
`gh auth setup-git`), never a token in a URL or a file. Repos: @@{repo_githubs}.

### Set up

Clone the hub into the folder that will hold the project, then let `./hub setup` do the rest:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/@@{project_hub_repo}.git
cd @@{project_hub_dir}
./hub setup
```

`./hub setup` clones the missing repos (@@{repo_dirs}) at `../<dir>` and fetches the others; if `hub.json` leaves your
identity unset, it asks before writing it from git config to `hub.local.json` (`--yes` skips asking). It prints one
`ok`/`missing` line per tool, credential and repo, each with its fix, then runs `./hub doctor`. Safe to run again.

- Identity: `hub.local.json` (gitignored), else `hub.json`, else your git config (see `./hub setup` above).
- @@{join_tracker_credential}

Then, from the hub directory, run `./agent` and type `/kickoff`: its first line says whether the hub's guard is on.

### Known traps

- uv older than 0.9 may offer only a Python 3.14 release candidate: run `uv self update` (in a cloud container,
  `pip install --user 'uv>=0.9'`), then check `uv --version`.
- macOS: `python3` and `git` come from the Xcode Command Line Tools; the first call offers to install them
  (`xcode-select --install` installs them directly).
- The hub's hooks and settings load only when the session starts in the hub directory: not in an app repo, not in
  the folder above the hub or a hub subfolder, not in a cloud session with the app repos attached. `/kickoff`
  probes the guard (`.claude/guard_probe.p12`) and says so loudly when it is off.@@{join_cloud}
